    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d80-a1">

                <pb facs="0242" n="1202" xml:id="pg1202"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 58.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Mariscal to Mr. Bragg.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-05-29"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 29,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Minister</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge
                    receipt of your excellency’s note of yesterday, with which you were pleased to
                    inclose copy of the instructions touching the case of A. K. Cutting, received
                    from the Hon. Mr. Bayard, under date of the 4th instant.</p>
                <p>In reply it gratifies me to advise your excellency that I shall carefully
                    consider the contents of the said instructions, coming as they do from the
                    Government of the United States, and in view of the question therein
                    treated.</p>
                <p>I renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Igno. Mariscal.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
